/* Calendar's date/time inputs (EventModal, TaskPanel) carry a literal
   `[color-scheme:dark]` utility so their native picker icon and dropdown
   chrome read correctly against the (then only) dark theme. Left alone, that
   forces a dark-styled calendar/clock glyph onto what is now a plain white
   `.input` in light mode. Match the surface it is actually sitting on instead
   of the hardcoded scheme — `.nx-dark-island` below still wants real dark
   chrome and is excluded the same way the rules above are. */
html[data-theme="light"] [class*="color-scheme:dark"]:not(.nx-dark-island, .nx-dark-island *) {
  color-scheme: light;
}

